x90baker99@gw.wmich.edu writes:

>Hey all,
>I have a question about omega...i think it will apply to any version...
>what does one sacrifice to one's god?  All i get is my stuff cursed that i
>try to sacrifice...corpses, items, whatever...its weird...

*omega spoiler warning* (smirk)



The higher the value of the item the greater the chance that he will accept
your sacrifice.  You will get a weird message and the item will dissappear from
your inventory.  NOTE: The USEFULNESS of the item is unimportant.  A dagger +16
(low value) would be rejected, even though its a very nice weapon.

>um also how does
>one uncurse items? I have tried scrolls of blessing and just get a message
>that the item is sufficiently evil to ward off the blessing or some such..

Use scrolls of blessing on uncursed items to get it blessed and with an
additonal +1 added to its enchantment.  To remove cursed items you need to
sacrifice an item to your god then request a blessing at your altar.
(Though you shouldn't ever be using a cursed item, have EVERYTHING either
identified at the thieves guild or with the spell or scroll)

